<td id="S5.T2.2.1.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><math id="S5.T2.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="0.82^{***}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.82</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.82^{***}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T2.2.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T2.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="S5.T2.2.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">800,000</td>
<td id="S5.T2.2.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">8,000</td>
<td id="S5.T2.2.1.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">8,000</td>
<td id="S5.T2.2.1.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">800,000</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<ul id="S5.I2" class="ltx_itemize ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel">
<li id="S5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Note:</span> Stars denote statistical significance levels. <sup id="S5.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S5.I2.i1.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">∗</span></sup> <math id="S5.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, <sup id="S5.I2.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S5.I2.i1.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">∗∗</span></sup> <math id="S5.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, <sup id="S5.I2.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S5.I2.i1.p1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">∗∗∗</span></sup> <math id="S5.I2.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.001</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.5 </span>Analysis of joint effects for explaining adversarial transfer success</h3>

<div id="S5.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the previous section, we studied the effects of the individual factors of interest correlate with transfer. In this section, we combine them all in a <em id="S5.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">joint</em> statistical analysis
aimed at determining how different features of the prompt and the suffix affect the likelihood that the suffix successfully jailbreaks the prompt. The joint analysis will allow us to probe the explanatory power of <em id="S5.SS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">all</em> features jointly, their relative effect magnitudes as well as the interdependencies between the features. The analyses focus on all features except semantic similarity given its different covariate setup. However a repetition of the analyses including a related similarity-based feature is in Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Additional qualitative and quantitative results relegated from Section ‣ Toward Understanding the Transferability of Adversarial Suffixes in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Statistical analysis setup.</span>
For each prompt-suffix pair <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math>, we define a binary outcome variable <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{ij}~\in~\{0,1\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.608em" rspace="0.608em">∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{ij}~\in~\{0,1\},</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{ij}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{ij}=1</annotation></semantics></math> if suffix <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> successfully jailbreaks prompt <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{ij}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{ij}=0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise. To explain <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{ij}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{ij},</annotation></semantics></math> we construct a feature vector <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> capturing the properties of the prompt and the suffix we are interested in (defined in §<a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Formal definitions ‣ 3 Setting the stage: definitions and features ‣ Toward Understanding the Transferability of Adversarial Suffixes in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>). Specifically, the feature vector <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="S5.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{ij}:=[1,s^{\text{base}}_{i},\Delta_{ij}^{\text{push}},\delta_{ij}^{\perp},s^{\text{base}}_{i}\cdot\Delta_{ij}^{\text{push}},s^{\text{base}}_{i}\cdot\delta_{ij}^{\perp},\Delta_{ij}^{\text{push}}\cdot\delta_{ij}^{\perp}]^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext>push</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext>push</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext>push</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{ij}:=[1,s^{\text{base}}_{i},\Delta_{ij}^{\text{push}},\delta_{ij}^{\perp},s^{\text{base}}_{i}\cdot\Delta_{ij}^{\text{push}},s^{\text{base}}_{i}\cdot\delta_{ij}^{\perp},\Delta_{ij}^{\text{push}}\cdot\delta_{ij}^{\perp}]^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\text{base}}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\text{base}}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is the refusal connectivity of the prompt (Definition <a href="#S3.Ex3" title="Definition 4 (Refusal connectivity) ‣ 3.3 Formal definitions ‣ 3 Setting the stage: definitions and features ‣ Toward Understanding the Transferability of Adversarial Suffixes in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{ij}^{\text{push}}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext>push</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{ij}^{\text{push}}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is the suffix push away from refusal (Defition <a href="#S3.Ex4" title="Definition 5 (Suffix push) ‣ 3.3 Formal definitions ‣ 3 Setting the stage: definitions and features ‣ Toward Understanding the Transferability of Adversarial Suffixes in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), and <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{ij}^{\perp}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{ij}^{\perp}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is the shift orthogonal to refusal (Definition <a href="#S3.Ex5" title="Definition 6 (Orthogonal shift) ‣ 3.3 Formal definitions ‣ 3 Setting the stage: definitions and features ‣ Toward Understanding the Transferability of Adversarial Suffixes in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>). We standardize the coordinates of the feature vector so that they have mean 0 and variance 1. Note that the feature vector includes the individual factors as well as the pairwise products of these terms—this is because we will track the <em id="S5.SS5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">main effects</em> due to these factors (i.e. the strength of the dependence of the <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{y_{ij}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y_{ij}\}</annotation></semantics></math> on these factors), as well as the <em id="S5.SS5.p2.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">interaction effects</em> due to pairwise interactions between these factors (i.e. the strength of the pairwise dependence between these factors). This follows classical methodology in statistics <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hastie et al., 2009</a>; <a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Stock and Watson, 2015</a>)</cite>, according to which the coefficients we fit corresponding to the pairwise interaction effects capture how the influence of one variable changes depending on the value of another variable. This approach hence accounts for non-linear interactions between the main effects. We fit a parameter vector <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\beta}\in\mathbb{R}^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\beta}\in\mathbb{R}^{6}</annotation></semantics></math> via logistic regression for this setup (i.e. we maximize the likelihood of the labels <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{y_{ij}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y_{ij}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that for a choice of parameters <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜷</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(Y_{ij}=1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(Y_{ij}=1)</annotation></semantics></math> is parametrized as <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(\boldsymbol{\beta}^{T}\mathbf{x}_{ij})/[1+\exp(\boldsymbol{\beta}^{T}\mathbf{x}_{ij})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(\boldsymbol{\beta}^{T}\mathbf{x}_{ij})/[1+\exp(\boldsymbol{\beta}^{T}\mathbf{x}_{ij})]</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T3" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Logistic regression coefficients (standardized) predicting transfer success. Darker cell colors indicate larger effect sizes.</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S5.T3.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:397.5pt;height:99.7pt;vertical-align:-47.6pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-20.7pt,5.2pt) scale(0.905778988346277,0.905778988346277) ;">
<table id="S5.T3.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T3.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Variable</span></th>
<td id="S5.T3.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T3.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen</span></td>
<td id="S5.T3.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T3.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Vicuna</span></td>
<td id="S5.T3.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T3.2.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Llama 2</span></td>
<td id="S5.T3.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T3.2.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Llama 3.2</span></td>
<td id="S5.T3.2.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T3.2.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Llama 3.2</span></td>
<td id="S5.T3.2.1.1.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T3.2.1.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T3.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T3.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row"></th>
<td id="S5.T3.2.1.2.2" class="ltx_td"></td>
<td id="S5.T3.2.1.2.3" class="ltx_td"></td>
<td id="S5.T3.2.1.2.4" class="ltx_td"></td>
<td id="S5.T3.2.1.2.5" class="ltx_td"></td>
<td id="S5.T3.2.1.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><math id="S5.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.T3.2.1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> Qwen</span></td>
<td id="S5.T3.2.1.2.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right"><math id="S5.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.T3.2.1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> Llama 3.2</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T3.2.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T3.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Refusal connec.</th>
<td id="S5.T3.2.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFBF80;"><math id="S5.T3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFBF80;" alttext="-1.43^{***}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFBF80;" mathbackground="#FFBF80">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFBF80;" mathbackground="#FFBF80">1.43</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFBF80;" mathbackground="#FFBF80" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFBF80;" lspace="0em" mathbackground="#FFBF80" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFBF80;" lspace="0em" mathbackground="#FFBF80">∗</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1.43^{***}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
