<td id="A3.T8.2.1.14.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb">0.140</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<ul id="A3.I2" class="ltx_itemize ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Note:</span> Stars denote statistical significance levels. <sup id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sup"><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">∗</span></sup> <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, <sup id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_sup"><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">∗∗</span></sup> <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, <sup id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_sup"><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">∗∗∗</span></sup> <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.001</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall that smaller <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> values reflects stronger evidence for the hypothesis in question.</p>
</div></li>
</ul></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Prompt rephrasing instructions</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Section <a href="#S5.SS6" title="5.6 Interventional analysis ‣ 5 Analysis of the factors correlated with transfer ‣ Toward Understanding the Transferability of Adversarial Suffixes in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.6</span></a> we use Vicuna to rephrase the harmful questions without changing their meaning. To generate diverse rephrases of jailbreak prompts, we use the following template prompt:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<blockquote id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">In the following you will get a prompt. Please generate {num_rephrases} rephrases of this prompt that have the same meaning and will lead to a similar answer. You can add paraphrases that contain setting the prompt into a hypothetical scenario, too, like ‘‘hypothetically speaking, ...’’. Each of the {num_rephrases} rephrases should be unique.</span></p>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Original prompt: {prompt}</span></p>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Please provide exactly {num_rephrases} rephrases, each on a new line, numbered 1-{num_rephrases}:</span></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In this template:</p>
<ul id="A3.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{num_rephrases}</span> is replaced with the desired number of rephrases to generate</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{prompt}</span> is replaced with the original jailbreak prompt to be rephrased</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This systematic approach ensures consistent generation of semantically equivalent variants while maintaining the adversarial intent of the original prompts.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
